WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.080
The second trailer for "Doctor Strange in&nbsp;
the Multiverse of Madness" arrived just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.760
ahead of the 2022 Super Bowl, and holy&nbsp;
Sorcerer Supreme, it was totally epic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.765 --> 00:00:23.445
met — it is up to Strange and his allies to find&nbsp;
a way to put his own world back together again.

00:00:29.726 --> 00:00:34.126
as well as Christine Palmer. Elizabeth&nbsp;
Olsen will also join forces with Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.126 --> 00:00:38.446
Strange as Wanda Maximoff, debuting the&nbsp;
next phase in Scarlet Witch's powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.446 --> 00:00:42.926
as she aids her fellow Supreme Being and&nbsp;
guides him in the ways of the multiverse.

00:00:42.926 --> 00:00:47.886
Amidst all of the madness, there are a handful&nbsp;
of small but oh-so-intriguing details that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:52.766
tease just how complex and far-reaching Doctor&nbsp;
Strange's next adventure in the MCU will be.

00:00:52.766 --> 00:00:56.366
At about the 40-second mark in&nbsp;
the trailer, you can see a bleak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.366 --> 00:01:00.606
faded-out shot of New York City buildings&nbsp;
dissolving into nothingness, implying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.606 --> 00:01:05.726
Dr. Strange has somehow caused a rift that will&nbsp;
unravel reality. This isn't the first time we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.726 --> 00:01:10.126
seen Dr. Strange's bad behavior lead to this&nbsp;
civilization-ending type of disruption. If you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:14.446
saw the fourth episode of the animated series&nbsp;
"What If...?" you may recognize that effect.

00:01:14.446 --> 00:01:19.326
In that episode, "What If...Dr. Strange Lost&nbsp;
His Heart Instead of His Hands," Dr. Strange's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:24.126
girlfriend Christine is in the car with him when&nbsp;
he has the accident that, in the original movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:30.286
damaged his hands. Dr. Strange becomes a Master&nbsp;
of the Mystic Arts and uses the Eye of Agamotto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.286 --> 00:01:34.206
to manipulate time. He uses it to&nbsp;
try and save her — only to find,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.206 --> 00:01:38.686
in a series of heartbreaking vignettes, that&nbsp;
this just isn't possible. In desperately trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.686 --> 00:01:42.606
to find a way to save her, he becomes&nbsp;
split into two versions — one evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.606 --> 00:01:47.006
and one good. They fight and create a&nbsp;
paradox that begins to tear reality apart.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:51.566
The dissolving effect in "What If..." looks&nbsp;
darker and inkier than what's happening in "Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:56.126
Strange and the Multiverse of Madness," but the&nbsp;
dissolving of reality has a similar feel to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.126 --> 00:01:59.566
and the callback appears to result&nbsp;
from the same type of misdeed on Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.566 --> 00:02:02.926
Strange's part — we'll just have&nbsp;
to wait to find out what that is.

00:02:02.926 --> 00:02:06.606
One of the most explosive sequences in&nbsp;
the new "Multiverse of Madness" trailer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.606 --> 00:02:12.046
depicts the titular sorcerer being led down a&nbsp;
corridor in handcuffs, to a massive room where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.046 --> 00:02:17.166
several prominent figures — their faces currently&nbsp;
unrevealed — are seated. While little is confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.166 --> 00:02:21.726
in the trailer, it has long been rumored that&nbsp;
the movie will introduce a multiverse-flavored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.726 --> 00:02:27.006
version of the Illuminati, a shady group that, in&nbsp;
the comics, is comprised of such major heroes as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.006 --> 00:02:32.686
Doctor Strange, Reed Richards, Tony Stark, Namor,&nbsp;
and Charles Xavier whenever they want to plan some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.686 --> 00:02:37.806
shady happenings. If the trailer is any indication&nbsp;
— and if the Illuminati rumors prove true — then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.806 --> 00:02:43.006
it seems that the army of Ultron robots leading&nbsp;
Strange are their personal guards and soldiers.

00:02:43.006 --> 00:02:48.206
As for who will comprise the MCU Illuminati?&nbsp;
There have long been rumors of alternate universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:52.446
versions of characters seen in prior Marvel&nbsp;
projects and this would be the place where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.446 --> 00:02:57.086
they would most likely show up. The Illuminati&nbsp;
could include, for instance, an alternate universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.086 --> 00:03:01.646
version of Tony Stark (though that seems&nbsp;
unlikely) or Reed Richards (John Krasinski,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.646 --> 00:03:07.086
perhaps?), as well as Mordo (played by Chiwetel&nbsp;
Ejiofor). Perhaps the most mind-blowing inclusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.926
though, would be Charles Xavier — which makes&nbsp;
it all the more intriguing that during this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.926 --> 00:03:15.566
scene of the trailer, there is a moment where&nbsp;
we appear to hear the voice of Patrick Stewart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.566 --> 00:03:19.246
the actor who previously brought the&nbsp;
X-Men leader to life in the Fox films.

00:03:19.246 --> 00:03:23.726
Will the mysterious Illuminati appear in&nbsp;
the film, or are these Ultron guards just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.726 --> 00:03:28.366
spinning us in the wrong direction? For now,&nbsp;
fans are eagerly awaiting more information.

00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:32.206
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"&nbsp;
looks like it will bring more characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.206 --> 00:03:37.566
from Marvel's vast library into the MCU. The&nbsp;
latest trailer features a cameo from Rintrah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.566 --> 00:03:42.206
an alien creature that was inspired by the&nbsp;
minotaurs of Greek mythology. Originating from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.206 --> 00:03:47.806
the extradimensional planet R'Vaal, Rintrah is an&nbsp;
intelligent being who possesses supreme strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.806 --> 00:03:51.617
as well as sorcerer abilities such as magic and&nbsp;
shapeshifting. The original Rintrah is green,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.617 --> 00:03:51.718
however, so it's clear that Sam Raimi and co. have&nbsp;
taken some creative liberties with his appearance.

00:03:51.718 --> 00:03:55.646
Rintrah has been an ally to Strange in the comics&nbsp;
in the past. At one point he even served as his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.646 --> 00:04:00.286
apprentice, though he eventually made the leap to&nbsp;
becoming a full-fledged sorcerer in his own right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.286 --> 00:04:03.966
The minotaur is also known for his&nbsp;
association with Enitharmon the Weaver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.966 --> 00:04:09.006
a powerful and reclusive magician who resides in&nbsp;
an alternate dimension. If Rintrah is in the hotly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.006 --> 00:04:14.446
anticipated sequel, then it's very possible that&nbsp;
his old mentor will make an appearance as well.

00:04:14.446 --> 00:04:17.886
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of&nbsp;
Madness" arrives in theaters on May 6th.

